.github/

# Platform-specific build outputs
android/
ios/
linux/
macos/
windows/

backend/backend
backend/go.mod
backend/go.sum
backend/localhost:8080
backend/uploads/
.env
# Local sqlite database — regenerated by the seed command.
# Keep it out of history: binary diffs aren't reviewable and they
# risk leaking test data into the repo.
backend/*.db
.metadata
pubspec.lock
# Admin auth keys are generated locally via `go run ./cmd/keygen`
# and uploaded through the admin gate; never commit them.
*.key
*.pub

# ============================================================================
# Docker stack runtime artifacts (docker/ in repo)
# ============================================================================
# Local env file for compose — contains secrets (POSTGRES_PASSWORD,
# CF_TUNNEL_TOKEN, ADMIN_PUBLIC_KEY). Template lives at docker/.env.example.
docker/.env

# Local backups emitted by docker/backup.sh
docker/data/
data/

# Bind-mount leftovers if someone ever swaps named volume → bind-mount
docker/uploads/

# Compiled Go binaries. Sources live in `backend/cmd/<name>/main.go` and
# are rebuilt via `go run ./cmd/<name>` (or `go build -o <name> ./cmd/<name>`
# if a binary is actually needed). Keep the binaries out of git history:
# they're large, un-reviewable ELF blobs and they leak Go toolchain
# version skew between contributors.
backend/keygen
backend/admincurl
backend/cmd/*/keygen
backend/cmd/*/admincurl

# Personal dev tooling / MCP config / Playwright artifacts. These come
# from local Claude Code / Playwright runs and have no place in the
# shared repo. The MCP config is a JSON file the user copies into their
# home directory if they want the same MCP servers enabled.
.mcp.json
.playwright-mcp/
